extends Object

# What the alien thinks these words mean.
#
# Not a dictionary. A working guess, in his own voice, written down at the
# moment he first got the shape of a word - which is why several of them are
# wrong, and wrong in the specific way a person guessing would be wrong:
# "ihnen" reads as "him", "daijoubu" reads as yes when it is frequently no,
# and "ahorita" does not mean now.
#
# There were three tables, holding eighty-six words between them, and
# GameState.word_guesses() returned the GERMAN one for any language that was
# not English or Turkish. So a player in Tokyo opened the journal and every
# Japanese word they had learned was looked up in a notebook of German and
# came back blank. Every word the game can teach now has a guess: nothing the
# player learns is left as a bare word with a progress bar under it.
#
# Part one: the languages of the first act, plus the two the story returns to.

